# zero / zero is a NaN that arithmetic has made: its sign stays, and that of a NaN out of bytes does not. Behind the return nobody can tell the two apart, so each return makes of its NaN what is to be made of it.
# CHECK-NOT: ImpureDouble
# CHECK: f4 Direct ({{*}}:Double, {{*}}:Boolean, {{*}}:Double) -> ({{*}}:Double)
# CHECK-NOT: ImpureDouble
